    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1947-01-20">January 20, 1947</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Sir:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>In reference to <rs ref="L11035" type="letter">your letter of January 14th</rs> I
                    would like to give you information about <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2690"
                        type="person">Miss Mary Jacker</rs>.</p>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2690" type="person">Miss Mary
                        Jacker</rs> since her arrival in the <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__684"
                        type="place">United States</rs> although I have seen her as a small
                    child-being her Godfather. She comes from a highly cultured family. For 25 years
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__963" type="person">her father</rs> is a close
                    friend of mine. Upon her arrival I had a few conversations with <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__2690" type="person">Mary</rs>, she made an
                    excellent impression on me. She is intelligent, modest and very eager to learn
                    and to adapt in this country. I do not hesitate to recommend her strongly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed><rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Paul
                        Tillich</rs><lb/>Professor at Union Theological Seminary, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
